# Keep heavy, never-served runtime data out of the Vercel deployment.
#
# Vercel bundles the uploaded project into EACH serverless function (minus that
# function's excludeFiles), so as data/ grew, functions without a broad exclude
# (daily/weekly/storylines/topics/updates) bundled the whole tree and blew past
# Vercel's 250 MB unzipped function limit, freezing all deploys.
#
# None of the dirs below are read by any api/ function at request time or by the
# static build (scripts/vercel_build.py -> build_wiki.py + render_static_pages.py).
# feed.js/rss.js/share.js touch tier1/runs only via graceful-fallback paths that
# degrade to tier1/latest.json when the runs are absent. Everything here stays in
# git (audit/replay) but ships out of the deployment.
data/raw
data/tier1/runs
data/llm
data/health
data/digest
data/diagnostics
data/cache
data/analysis
